// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
//
// DomaSettingsProviderRRO -- Bluetooth starts off on a fresh /data.
//
// SettingsProvider seeds Settings.Global bluetooth_on from def_bluetooth_on once, on the
// first boot of an empty /data, and the Settings toggle keeps the user's choice from
// then on. CarSettingsProviderConfigRRO sets def_bluetooth_on=true
// (packages/services/Car/car_product/rro/overlay-config/SettingsProviderRRO/res/values/
// defaults.xml:24), and a build-time DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS value loses to any runtime
// overlay: on a fresh RPi4 /data (2026-09-24) bluetooth_on came up 1 and
// `cmd overlay lookup` resolved def_bluetooth_on to true, with the device overlay saying
// false.
//
// Static overlays are applied in partition order (PackagePartitions: system, vendor, odm,
// oem, product, system_ext) and, within one partition, by android:priority
// (OverlayConfig.java, sStaticOverlayComparator); the last one applied wins. Car's RRO is
// in product with no priority, i.e. 0, so this is a product RRO at priority 1. A vendor
// RRO would lose whatever its priority. Signed with the platform key, like Car's.
runtime_resource_overlay {
    name: "DomaSettingsProviderRRO",
    resource_dirs: ["res"],
    certificate: "platform",
    product_specific: true,
}
